WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.320
Hey, how's it going bros, my name is PewDiePie!

00:00:02.320 --> 00:00:08.500
Just wanted to make a quick video to say thanks. I know it's a bit redundant ... ahh okay.

00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:12.640
But I realized that I never really got a chance to fully express my gratitude,

00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:16.700
For... all the support that I've gotten throughout these past couple days

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:19.600
I don't think I've gotten this much support... EVER

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:23.400
Of- of me making videos, these past six years on Youtube.

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:27.880
And, it really turned this shitty situation completely around,

00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:32.460
And all the support that I've been getting from you guys has just been incredible!

00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:38.320
It seemed that people that doesn't even necessarily consume my content came to support me,

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:43.280
Throughout this whole thing with the media because they thought the whole situation was unjustified.

00:00:43.420 --> 00:00:46.860
If theres uh, any newcomers.. Aha! Ahh.. uhh..

00:00:46.860 --> 00:00:47.840
Domo Arigato!

00:00:47.860 --> 00:00:49.940
Thank you very much! [laughs]

00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:52.060
Why- Why am I awkward in- in..?

00:00:52.060 --> 00:00:55.220
I also didn't realize how much it would mean to me,

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:56.900
The fact that so many people supported me,

00:00:56.980 --> 00:00:58.620
because I-I didn't think I'd need it.

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:03.960
But when it seems like the whole world is kinda turned against you and- and is after blood,

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:09.340
To have people defending you, uh even when you haven't gotten the chance to defend yourself,

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:11.240
It really means a lot.

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:14.700
It- It's something that, I know I will never forget.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:17.560
It was- It was almost like the internet had my back

00:01:17.820 --> 00:01:22.420
throughout this whole situation and uh, that has just been so.. incredibly cool

00:01:22.660 --> 00:01:25.340
'Cause that's really all I care about.

00:01:25.360 --> 00:01:29.740
Um, I didn't make my way to where I am thanks to the media,

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:32.420
I didn't get where I am through them.

00:01:32.420 --> 00:01:37.540
I- I made my way through the internet and, and through you guys. And thanks to you guys watching me,

00:01:37.940 --> 00:01:43.040
And, if you guys are still supporting me, that means everything to me

00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:46.480
Like I couldn't care less what the media thinks about me and what they say about me,

00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:50.360
And it clearly, all bridges are seemed 
almost burnt at this point, [laughs]

00:01:50.760 --> 00:01:53.240
But the fact that you guys, had my back,

00:01:53.240 --> 00:01:54.200
It means everything.

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:58.400
Um.. It- It's because I- uh, I-... I saw this coming.

00:01:58.760 --> 00:02:02.420
I said it in a video earlier this year I think what i said was something like;

00:02:02.420 --> 00:02:06.360
2017 is the year it's gonna go bad for me

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:08.620
Alright, I'm just calling it out right now.

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:11.190
Uh- You want you, get out before you can,

00:02:11.190 --> 00:02:14.340
Cause PewDiePie is-... He's a bad boy now,

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:17.200
Anti- anti-Semitic! What other labels can we put him-?

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:18.680
Hitler loving!

00:02:18.680 --> 00:02:22.940
The media wants to paint me as some sort of villain

00:02:23.180 --> 00:02:27.380
So it went a lot faster and a lot harder

00:02:27.380 --> 00:02:30.540
than i thought but I knew it was going to happen

00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:33.340
because I-I let all guards down

00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:35.180
Like I've been so tired of

00:02:35.180 --> 00:02:38.880
everything that I say being taken out of context,

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:40.680
Like even before and I- it's

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:42.870
almost like I have to think what I say

00:02:42.870 --> 00:02:44.459
now in every single video because

00:02:44.459 --> 00:02:46.349
someone else might watch it that isn't

00:02:46.349 --> 00:02:48.390
necessarily my audience and they might

00:02:48.390 --> 00:02:50.370
take that one part out of it and put it

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:52.799
on a headline and it's just so stupid

00:02:52.799 --> 00:02:55.920
but I realized I'm not going to censor

00:02:55.920 --> 00:02:58.319
myself for that. I-I should care about

00:02:58.319 --> 00:03:00.480
the ones that actually watch my content

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:02.489
and what they think about it an- and I

00:03:02.489 --> 00:03:04.890
think if anything that's been more clear

00:03:04.890 --> 00:03:07.200
and obvious to me than ever

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:10.960
Obviously I'm not going to see this as some way to kind of provoke or...

00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:12.360
...start drama.

00:03:12.360 --> 00:03:15.740
I have really, REALLY no intentions in doing that

00:03:15.740 --> 00:03:16.980
There's been those so much

00:03:16.980 --> 00:03:20.040
with the drama with the media these past couple of months

00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:21.359
but it's really not some...

00:03:21.360 --> 00:03:23.960
It's not something I thrive on

00:03:23.960 --> 00:03:25.500
It's not something that I feel like;

00:03:25.500 --> 00:03:27.180
"What can I do next?!"

00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:28.889
If- if anything what I realized about

00:03:28.889 --> 00:03:30.140
this whole thing is that,

00:03:30.140 --> 00:03:34.760
I really, really, really just care about entertaining my audience

00:03:34.760 --> 00:03:36.060
Uh, a lot of people have been

00:03:36.060 --> 00:03:38.609
saying "Oh, well he lost so much, he lost

00:03:38.609 --> 00:03:40.739
his show and all these things", but

00:03:40.739 --> 00:03:42.569
all these things are possible and if

00:03:42.569 --> 00:03:44.880
anything now I'm independent for the

00:03:44.880 --> 00:03:46.950
first time in four years or five years

00:03:46.950 --> 00:03:50.560
and uh I feel great! I feel really really

00:03:50.580 --> 00:03:53.460
excited about what opportunities that's going to bring in

00:03:53.480 --> 00:03:56.620
and, uhh, if I didn't know better, I would say thank you

00:03:56.620 --> 00:03:58.200
to the Wall Street Journal.

00:03:58.240 --> 00:04:01.320
Actually, t-thank you, Wall Street Journal! [Laughs]

00:04:01.320 --> 00:04:05.040
There's been some real busy couple of days for me and I'm sorry

00:04:05.040 --> 00:04:07.049
if the content hasn't really been up to

00:04:07.049 --> 00:04:10.049
standard but I feel more committed and

00:04:10.049 --> 00:04:12.870
more passionate than- [Burps]

00:04:12.870 --> 00:04:15.150
I want to do something bigger about this

00:04:15.150 --> 00:04:17.760
whole thing but I-I can't say what it is

00:04:17.760 --> 00:04:19.769
but that's for the future but anyway

00:04:19.769 --> 00:04:21.659
what I want to say is you guys fucking

00:04:21.659 --> 00:04:22.260
rock!

00:04:22.260 --> 00:04:24.960
You- you- you, you're fucking awesome! I... I

00:04:24.960 --> 00:04:28.980
feel like I don't deserve it, but uh- uh thank you! Thank you very much!

00:04:28.980 --> 00:04:29.760
I'm ready to

00:04:29.760 --> 00:04:32.360
keep making videos and uh love you!

00:04:32.380 --> 00:04:34.460
Also by the way...

00:04:35.540 --> 00:04:37.540
JK Rowling is still a Cu-

